Z||000000||ur2biteme||10-17-2000||08:57 PM||||i guess california and GM teamed up in their efforts in getting fieros off the road.  i pull into the smog station today, we go over all the info, and guess what?  my car is considered a high risk of being a gross polluter due to it's high mileage status.  they tell me that i have to go to a smog only station (i guess that's the replacement for the referee stations?)<P>anyways, i get there, odometer reads 170,769.  excuse me, just checked the worksheet my vehicle fits a "high emitter profile".  i get over there, kinda worried, even though i just replaced the cat converter yesterday.  they put it on the machine, and not only did it pass, but it was WAY below average on everything but the hydrocarbon test.  even that was barely above average, but still WAY below the maximum.  <P>heh this car has been nothing but spectacular with the crap it's been through, and even though i paid way too much for it than it's worth because of the body damage, it's still hung around like a champ with all the crap i put it through.  yeah, all this even though it fits the description of vehicles that are typically in the top 15% worst poluters in CA.  heh.  sorry CA and GM, but you arent getting this one off the road.  heh.<P>that and i get home and i finally got the new E-brake cables (thanks 87ec05) in the mail.  gonna try to get them on tonight, that is, if i'm not lazy.  oh, 87ec05, i guess your car would fit the same description as mine if you had a ton of miles on yours too.  heh.  just remember that if you plan on moving to CA.  lol.  <P>sorry bout the bandwidth   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-17-2000||11:23 PM||||My own fiero passed DE emmisions easily. Like yours the machine spit up numbers way way below max. (near zero for most.)<P>You have to remember that those guidelines are based on the typically neglected cars on the road today.<P>A perfect example.... Go around a parking lot for 5 minutes and see how many cars have flat tires. I don't mean just a little low. I mean running on the sidewalls low. I had at 3 like that at work yesterday. A bunch more were visibly low.(out of about 30-40 cars. Even the real expecive cars were low.)<P>According to the print version of Quaker States "reformulated to protect beyond 3000..." ad the USDOT estimates the average oil change interval is over 5600 miles. (I haven't had time to verify that.) I'd believe it. I bet it is really even higher than that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ur2biteme||10-17-2000||11:37 PM||||yeah.  i'd agree.  i even see the cars with real low tires myself (mine can get that way from time to time, but i check mine and fill periodically).  it's just that it seemed (and still does) like the state is singling out this car for some reason.  not only because of the smog stuff (you know, having to go to a special station), but they never sent my registration paperwork.  <P>hopefully when i give my DMV some "info" tomorrow about my situation, i'll get some results.  oh well, my car did it's part, now it's time for me to do mine.....<P>oh, i don't know how stringent other state inspections are, but i know that CA is one of, if not the strictest states.  that's why i'm so pleased.  <P>i've never owned a car with this many miles.  also, as you may have been able to see from my experiences with my truck, this is one of the more lively car for its age that i've had the pleasure of owning.  good thing they don't freak about oil leaks for inspections here.  i'd have been up s___ creek.  lol<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||10-18-2000||02:37 AM||||I went through this exact thing about a year ago.  Initially it failed, but only marginally.  Later, I removed the cat and found it was efectively empty (except for a coupe of pebble sized pieces).  I put a new cat on it and it not only passed, but it barely registered on any of the tests.  I just wish they would get rid of the visual inspection so I can put an supercharger on it without a big hassle.<BR>||||reg||1
